KNOWNBUG (parser): N5008 [temp.names]/5.  The `template` keyword before a member
template-id is only required for a dependent nested-name-specifier; for a
non-dependent class-template-id such as `C<int>` it is optional.  CBMC's parser
rejects `C<int>::al<char>::value` (parse error before '> :: value') but accepts
`C<int>::template al<char>::value`.  The bug fires for a member alias template
and a nested class template alike, needs only a single inner argument, and
requires the outer name to be a class-template-id (a non-template outer class
parses fine).  This is the shape of libstdc++'s
`_TupleConstraints<_Types...>::__constructible<_UTypes...>` (written WITH the
keyword there, so std::tuple does not hit it).  Flip to CORE once the parser
accepts a member template-id after a non-dependent class-template-id without the
`template` keyword.
